**Section 21 of the Marine Products Export Development Authority (MPEDA) Act, 1972** deals with **“Power to make rules”**.

### Key Provisions:

> **Section 21. Power to make rules**

> *(1)* The Central Government may, by notification in the Official Gazette, make rules for carrying out the purposes of this Act and for regulating the activities of the Authority under this Act.

> *(2)* The Central Government may also make rules for the regulation of marine products trade, including matters relating to:
>
